mode: "100644"
text: "# The HUMAN framework — avatar video with human standards\n\nThe presenter is synthetic; the standards stay human. Each letter is a gate; most avatar failures happen at H\n(an avatar where a real face belonged) or M (essay prose read by a robot).\n\n## H — Have a reason for an avatar\nThe fit test before anything renders. **Avatar-right:** training/onboarding, explainers, FAQ/support,\nlocalization at scale, faceless educational series, high-volume consistency (the presenter never has a bad\nday). **Avatar-wrong:** trust-led founder content, testimonials, emotionally-nuanced persuasion — avatars read\npolished-but-clinical, and the parasocial trust those formats build comes from a real human → route to\n`talking-head-and-piece-to-camera`. The hybrid is the pro move: the founder films the trust layer; the avatar\nscales the informational layer.\n\n## U — Use consented likeness only\nThe consent architecture is the point, not friction: stock avatars are real paid actors who agreed; a personal\navatar requires **your** live consent recording (same person as the source media; single-take source, never\nspliced). **Never** an avatar of a competitor, celebrity, politician, or anyone who hasn't verifiably\nconsented — impersonation and fake endorsements are prohibited by the platform and by this stack. Governance:\nshare the avatar's outfits/spaces, keep edit rights and the voice with the owner.\n\n## M — Make the script spoken-word\n**The script is most of avatar quality.** Write for the ear: short sentences, contractions, one idea per\nsentence, conversational rhythm — never essay prose pasted into the script box. Use SSML for pauses,\npronunciation, and emphasis; pick the voice + emotional register deliberately; frame the avatar closer\n(lip-sync reads better per the docs). **Lock the copy before generating:** a comma-level edit forces a full\n~8–12-min re-render that eats the minute cap — read it aloud, get sign-off, then render once.\n\n## A — Assemble scenes + localize\nBrand kit + template once → scenes with B-roll (the AI Playground — use the Veo 3.1 lane; the Sora API\nsunsets Sept 24 2026), screen recordings,\ninteractivity (quizzes/hotspots) where the format earns it. **Localization is the superpower:** lock the\nmaster → 1-click translation / AI dubbing (voice-clone consistency across languages) → **a native-speaker QA\npass per language** (machine translation is a draft, not a deliverable) → localized on-screen text + subtitles.\nOne master, tracked variants — never twenty divergent scripts.\n\n## N — Note the disclosure + publish\nA synthetic presenter is **disclosed, always**: YouTube's altered-content label, TikTok's AI tag, the EU AI\nAct's synthetic-media obligations (from Aug 2026), C2PA provenance where available. Then the human approves the\nvideo, export → `capcut` if captions/pace need work → `scheduling-and-queue` → **WoopSocial publishes** the\nfinished file (it does not generate avatars). Build deadline buffer — render/audio-sync failures are reported\nnear deadlines; regulated topics may sit in 12–24h moderation review.\n"
